Using your custom KDTree:

1) Create an enum for PickupType
	a. Invalid, Health, WeaponAmmo, Coins, Upgrade, SpecialItem

2) Create a class PickUp
	a. PickupType mType;
	b. std::string mName;
		i. Stores the name of the pickup
	c. Vector3 mPosition;
		i. Location where the item is in the world
	d. Pickup(PickupType pickupType, const Vector3& pos)
		i. Constructor that stores the pickupType
		ii. Use the pickupType to set the name

3) Create a class PickupManager
	a. Contains a Vector of Pickups
	b. Contains a KDTree to reuse in searches
	c. void AddItem(PickupType pickupType, const Vector3& pos)
		i. Adds an item to the pickups and stores the position
		ii. Stores the pickup in the KDTree<float, 3>
	d. const Pickup* GetClosestPickup(const Vector3& pos)
		i. Do a search to find the closest item to the position
	e. void ObtainPickupsInRange(const Vector3& pos, float range, PickupType pickupType)
		i. Do a search to find all items within a given range
		ii. Use the pickupType to find a specific item, if Invalid, get all pickups in range

4) Main flow
	a. Create 100 random pickups in various positions
	b. Create a Vector3 for “player”
	c. Player has an “attract range” where pickups within 10.0f are picked up
		i. Give a player a set position, print all items picked up in range and their locations
	d. Player is low on health, find all the health pickups withing 50.0f to identify
		i. Print the health pickups names as well as the location
	e. Player has just started the game and is looking for a pickup, find the closest pickup
		i. Print the pickup name as well as location from the player